# Architecture

Feature layout (only create folders that the feature needs):

```text
lib/features/<feature>/
  domain/entities|repositories|usecases
  data/models|mappers|datasources|repositories
  presentation/pages|widgets|forms
  presentation/viewmodels|providers     # Riverpod
  presentation/cubits|blocs            # BLoC
lib/core/   # network, errors, router, theme, storage, session, widgets
```

Dependency direction: Presentation → Domain ← Data. Domain never imports Flutter, Dio, JSON, Isar, or `data/`.

| Layer | Owns | Must not |
|---|---|---|
| Domain | Entity, repository contract, UseCase | DTO, Dio, Widgets, BuildContext |
| Data | DTO, Mapper, Api, DataSource, repository impl | Widgets, BuildContext, business rules |
| Presentation | Page, controller (ViewModel **or** Cubit/Bloc), Widget, Form | Repository impl, Api, DTO |

```dart
// BAD — page talks to data
remoteDataSource.fetch();

// GOOD — page talks to the presentation controller; controller talks to UseCase
await controller.load();
```

- One feature does not import another feature's `data/` or widgets. Share via `lib/core/` or Domain contracts.
- DTO never leaves Data. Outside Data, use Entity.
- The presentation controller never calls Api/DataSource. If UseCases exist, it does not call the repository directly.
- Reuse `lib/core/` (ApiClient, ErrorMapper, FailureHandler, GoRouter, SessionStorage). Do not duplicate it inside a feature.
- State stack is Riverpod **or** BLoC (`state-management.mdc`). Never both.
